---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import { BOOKS } from '../data/books.mjs';
import { thumb } from '../data/images.mjs';

const speakingEvents = (await getCollection('speaking')).sort(
	(a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf(),
);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`Speaking | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Magnus Oxenwaldt's speaking engagements on AI strategy, digital transformation, and enterprise architecture." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />

		<section class="speak-hero">
			<div class="speak-hero-inner">
				<p class="kicker">Speaking</p>
				<h1>Keynotes &amp; executive briefings</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Talks on AI strategy, digital transformation, and the systems-thinking
					behind durable enterprise change. Available worldwide for keynotes,
					panels, and board off-sites.
				</p>
				<a href="mailto:magnus@oxenwaldt.com?subject=Speaking%20enquiry" class="btn-primary">Enquire about speaking</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<main class="speak-main">
			<section class="keynotes">
				<h2>Signature keynotes</h2>
				<p class="section-lede">Each one is built on a book, so the room leaves with the argument and the tools behind it.</p>
				<div class="keynote-grid">
					<article class="keynote">
						<img src={BOOKS[0].cover} alt="" width={BOOKS[0].coverSize[0]} height={BOOKS[0].coverSize[1]} loading="lazy" />
						<div>
							<h3>AI won't fix your company</h3>
							<p class="from">From <a href={`/books#${BOOKS[0].slug}`}><em>{BOOKS[0].title}</em></a></p>
							<p>The question isn't whether to use AI. It's what your organisation must become when intelligence is suddenly abundant. Strategy, governance, architecture, adoption and measurement, and a plan for the first ninety days. For boards and executive teams.</p>
						</div>
					</article>
					<article class="keynote">
						<img src={BOOKS[1].cover} alt="" width={BOOKS[1].coverSize[0]} height={BOOKS[1].coverSize[1]} loading="lazy" />
						<div>
							<h3>AI won't make you smarter. The partnership will.</h3>
							<p class="from">From <a href={`/books#${BOOKS[1].slug}`}><em>{BOOKS[1].title}</em></a></p>
							<p>Who you have to become when a digital coworker does the work you used to do. How to brief it, how to read work you did not watch being made, and how to stay the accountable half. For leaders and knowledge workers.</p>
						</div>
					</article>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="topics">
				<h2>Other topics</h2>
				<div class="topics-grid">
					<div class="topic">
						<h3>AI strategy &amp; implementation</h3>
						<p>From pilot to production. Practical frameworks for enterprise AI adoption that deliver measurable ROI — not pitches, but patterns drawn from real engagements.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="topic">
						<h3>Digital transformation</h3>
						<p>Leading change through technology adoption. Capability building, change management, and where the real friction lives.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="topic">
						<h3>Enterprise architecture</h3>
						<p>Building scalable systems with ERP, CRM, and AI integration in complex organizations. Where AI lives and gets governed.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="topic">
						<h3>AI in retail &amp; e-commerce</h3>
						<p>Industry-specific perspective on customer experience, operations optimization, and what agentic commerce changes.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			{speakingEvents.length > 0 && (
				<section class="events">
					<h2>Selected events</h2>
					<div class="event-list">
						{speakingEvents.map((event) => (
							<article class="event">
								{event.data.heroImage && (
									<div class="event-image"><img src={thumb(event.data.heroImage)} alt={event.data.title} loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
								)}
								<div class="event-body">
									<div class="event-meta">
										<span class="event-date">{event.data.date.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', year: 'numeric' })}</span>
										<span class="dot">·</span>
										<span>{event.data.event}</span>
										{event.data.featured && (<span class="pill">Featured</span>)}
									</div>
									<h3>{event.data.title}</h3>
									<p>{event.data.description}</p>
									<div class="event-foot">
										<span class="loc">📍 {event.data.location}</span>
										{event.data.tags && (
											<div class="tags">
												{event.data.tags.slice(0, 3).map((tag: string) => (<span class="tag">{tag}</span>))}
											</div>
										)}
									</div>
								</div>
							</article>
						))}
					</div>
				</section>
			)}

			{speakingEvents.length === 0 && (
				<section class="empty">
					<p>Upcoming events will be listed here.</p>
				</section>
			)}
			<section class="kit" id="speaker-kit">
				<h2>Speaker kit</h2>
				<p class="section-lede">For organisers and press. Use freely with credit.</p>
				<div class="kit-grid">
					<div class="bio-block">
						<h3>Short bio</h3>
						<p>Magnus Oxenwaldt is VP Group AI at Columbus Global, author of <em>AI Don't Fix Stupidity</em> and <em>AI Don't Make You Smarter</em>, and host of the <em>Future Bytes</em> podcast. He helps leaders turn AI from a slide into a system.</p>
						<h3>Long bio</h3>
						<p>Magnus Oxenwaldt is VP Group AI at Columbus Global, where he leads the AI practice and the company's own AI-first transformation. He has spent nearly thirty years in technology leadership: IT manager, eight years as CTO, five as Chief Commercial Officer, then executive consultant and enterprise architect across ERP, customer engagement and integration.</p>
						<p>He is the author of two books on AI at work. <em>AI Don't Fix Stupidity</em> asks what a company has to become when intelligence is suddenly abundant. <em>AI Don't Make You Smarter</em> asks who you have to become inside it. Every week he hosts <em>Future Bytes</em>, a podcast on the AI news that matters for business. He holds a master's degree in marketing economics.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="photos">
						<h3>Photos</h3>
						<a href="/images/magnus-oxenwaldt-2024-columbus.jpg" download><img src={thumb("/images/magnus-oxenwaldt-2024-columbus.jpg")} alt="Magnus Oxenwaldt, portrait" loading="lazy" /><span>Portrait ↓</span></a>
						<a href="/images/magnus_portrait_casual.png" download><img src={thumb("/images/magnus_portrait_casual.png")} alt="Magnus Oxenwaldt, casual portrait" loading="lazy" /><span>Casual ↓</span></a>
						<h3>Book covers</h3>
						{BOOKS.map((b) => (<a href={b.cover} download class="cover-dl">{b.title} ↓</a>))}
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="book-it"><a href="mailto:magnus@oxenwaldt.com?subject=Speaking%20enquiry" class="btn-primary">Book Magnus</a></p>
			</section>
		</main>

		<Footer />

		<style>
			.speak-hero {
				background: var(--cream);
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
				padding: 4rem 1.5rem 3rem;
			}
			.speak-hero-inner { max-width: 56rem; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; }
			.kicker {
				font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
				font-size: 0.78rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.18em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				color: var(--accent);
				margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
				font-weight: 600;
			}
			.speak-hero h1 {
				font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
				margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
				color: var(--ink);
				line-height: 1.1;
			}
			.lede {
				color: var(--text);
				margin: 0 auto 2rem;
				font-size: 1.1rem;
				line-height: 1.65;
				max-width: 38rem;
			}
			.btn-primary {
				display: inline-flex;
				background: var(--ink);
				color: var(--cream);
				padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
				border-radius: 6px;
				font-weight: 500;
				text-decoration: none;
				transition: background 0.2s;
			}
			.btn-primary:hover { background: var(--accent); color: var(--cream); }

			.speak-main { max-width: 56rem; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
			.topics { padding: 3.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
			.topics h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 2rem; color: var(--ink); }
			.keynotes { padding: 3.5rem 0 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
			.kit { padding: 3.5rem 0 4rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
			.keynotes h2, .kit h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--ink); }
			.section-lede { color: var(--text-muted); margin: -0.5rem 0 1.5rem; }
			.keynote-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; }
			.keynote { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 10px; background: #fff; }
			.keynote img { width: 7rem; height: auto; border-radius: 2px; box-shadow: var(--box-shadow-lg); }
			.keynote h3 { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.25; }
			.keynote .from { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
			.keynote p { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
			.kit-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; }
			.bio-block h3, .photos h3 { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem; }
			.photos a { display: inline-block; margin: 0 0.75rem 0.75rem 0; color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
			.photos img { display: block; width: 7rem; height: 7rem; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
			.photos .cover-dl { display: block; }
			.book-it { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
			.topics-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
				gap: 2rem;
			}
			.topic h3 {
				font-size: 1.2rem;
				margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
				color: var(--ink);
			}
			.topic p {
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-size: 0.98rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.events { padding: 3.5rem 0 4rem; }
			.events h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 2rem; color: var(--ink); }
			.event-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem; }
			.event {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: 12rem 1fr;
				gap: 2rem;
				align-items: flex-start;
				padding-bottom: 2rem;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
			}
			.event:last-child { border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: 0; }
			.event-image img {
				width: 100%;
				height: auto;
				aspect-ratio: 4/3;
				object-fit: cover;
				border-radius: 6px;
				border: 1px solid var(--rule);
			}
			.event-body { min-width: 0; }
			.event:not(:has(.event-image)) .event-body { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
			.event-meta {
				display: flex;
				gap: 0.5rem;
				font-size: 0.85rem;
				color: var(--text-muted);
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
				align-items: center;
			}
			.event-date { font-weight: 500; }
			.dot { color: var(--rule); }
			.pill {
				background: var(--accent);
				color: var(--cream);
				font-size: 0.72rem;
				font-weight: 500;
				padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
				border-radius: 9999px;
				letter-spacing: 0.04em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
			}
			.event h3 {
				font-size: 1.4rem;
				margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
				color: var(--ink);
				line-height: 1.25;
			}
			.event p { color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; line-height: 1.55; }
			.event-foot { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 0.88rem; }
			.loc { color: var(--text-muted); }
			.tags { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
			.tag {
				background: var(--cream-soft);
				border: 1px solid var(--rule);
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-size: 0.75rem;
				padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
				border-radius: 4px;
			}

			.empty { padding: 4rem 0; text-align: center; color: var(--text-muted); }

			@media (max-width: 720px) {
				.topics-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
				.keynote-grid, .kit-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
				.event { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
				.event-image img { aspect-ratio: 16/9; }
				.speak-hero { padding: 3rem 1rem 2.5rem; }
				.topics, .events { padding: 2.5rem 0; }
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
